      }

      <h2 id="related">Where to go next</h2>
      <p>If the racket is not your limiting factor, the next thing worth an evening's attention is where you are standing when the shuttle arrives: <a href="/guides/badminton-doubles-positioning">badminton doubles positioning</a> covers the two shapes and when to switch between them, and costs nothing.</p>
      <p>If you are kitting out a club rather than yourself, <a href="/guides/how-to-start-a-badminton-club">how to start a badminton club</a> deals with nets, posts, shuttles and what a hall actually needs.</p>

      <div style="margin-top:34px;padding-top:22px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)">
        <h4 style="margin:0 0 8px">How this guide was put together</h4>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.95rem;margin:0">ePegboard builds club-night software. We are not coaches, we do not sell rackets, and we have not tested one. <strong>We have no commercial relationship with any racket manufacturer or retailer, including the two whose catalogues we counted, and no link on this page earns us a commission.</strong> The performance claims here come from published research, the legal ones from the Laws of Badminton, and the market ones from our own count. Nothing here is medical advice.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.95rem;margin:12px 0 0"><strong>The count:</strong> on 23 August 2026 we read the public product feeds of <a href="https://www.badmintonhq.co.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Badminton HQ</a> and <a href="https://www.centralsports.co.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Central Sports</a>. Badminton HQ's catalogue gave <strong>228 adult single rackets</strong> after excluding 9 junior rackets and 6 multi-racket sets and training aids, and <strong>every market-structure figure quoted above is from that catalogue alone</strong>; Central Sports' 186 rackets were used only to check that the trends ran the same way, which they did. Prices are the lowest listed variant on the day, sale prices included, so they read low against list. Specifications are the retailers' own product tags, which describe how a racket is <em>marketed</em> rather than measurements we took. It is a one-day snapshot and we did not weigh, string or hit anything. Both feeds are public and the counts are reproducible; we will share the analysis scripts with anyone who asks.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.95rem;margin:12px 0 0"><strong>Sources:</strong> <a href="https://extranet.bwf.sport/docs/document-system/81/1466/1470/Section%204.1%20-%20Laws%20of%20Badminton%20-%2026%20April%202025%20V5.0%20(2)%20.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BWF Laws of Badminton, Law 4</a> (Section 4.1, V5.0, in force 26 April 2025) &middot; <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-023-37108-x" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Towler, Mitchell &amp; King (2023) on swingweight and shuttle speed</a> &middot; <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/02640414.2020.1792132" target="_blank" rel="noopener">McErlain-Naylor et al. (2020) on impact location</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.stuartmcnaylor.com/publication/wcrss19/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">King, Afzal &amp; McErlain-Naylor (2019) on impact location and head speed</a> &middot; <a href="https://revistaseug.ugr.es/index.php/IJRSS/article/view/33203" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Phomsoupha, Ibrahime &amp; Laffaye (2024) on shaft deflection</a> &middot; <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38761131/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Musculoskeletal injuries in badminton (2024 review)</a> &middot; <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16861576/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hatch et al. (2006) on tennis grip size and forearm muscle firing patterns</a> &middot; <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24646202/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rossi et al. (2014) on tennis grip size and lateral epicondylalgia risk</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.victor-europe.com/blog/article/how-to-pick-the-right-badminton-rackets-for-beginners" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Victor on choosing a beginner racket</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.ycsports.com/blogs/news/badminton-racket-balance-explained" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YC Sports on the 285/295 mm balance convention</a></p>
